refuted: "TWO CANDIDATES REFUTED, one verifier each. (1) correctness proposed as important that newestRead's in-flight drop plus no timeout on the shell's readers lets one hung adb or security freeze every quiet re-read; the verifier found a shown read always starts and supersedes the hung one (newestRead.ts:15, entering setup, choosing the emulator, every action through thenRead, supersede), the spinner stays visible, no wrong reading is shown, the drop is DEC-62's deliberate guard against stacking shell reads, and ran had no timeout on main either: a hypothetical hang with a recovery path, below important. (2) altitude proposed as important that the app sequences trust_simulators then set_proxy and install_on_emulators then route_emulators and picks open_route's payload by name; the verifier found the order deliberate and safe (trust first, so nothing routes to a store without the CA; a failure leaves a harmless, retryable state), set_up_this_machine atomic only for its single elevation prompt (F27), and the shell's tagged Route enum and mark validators fail closed on a wrong payload. The efficiency finder raised nothing: the 3 s watch is visibility-gated and single-flight, scans are memoized per refresh, the recordings load on demand."
